<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 18 April, from 796 to 1955.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">796 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,230 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Æthelred I of Northumbria is murdered</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Æthelred I was killed at Corbridge by his own nobles. His death, typical of Northumbria's violent politics, came three years after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raiders had sacked the monastery at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindisfarne">Lindisfarne</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1506 CE <span class="tih-ago">520 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius II lays the foundation stone of the new St Peter's</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a> laid the first stone of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donato-bramante">Bramante</a>'s new basilica in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Building took 120 years and drew on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a>, Maderno and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gian-lorenzo-bernini">Bernini</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/boston" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boston.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1775 CE <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paul Revere rides to warn of British troops</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Paul Revere and William Dawes rode from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> to warn that British regulars were marching to seize colonial arms. The first shots of the Revolutionary War were fired at dawn the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1906 CE <span class="tih-ago">120 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake and fire devastate San Francisco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.9 earthquake struck before dawn, and fires burned for three days. Some 3,000 people died and more than half the city's population was left homeless.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1923 CE <span class="tih-ago">103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yankee Stadium opens with a Babe Ruth home run</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Babe Ruth hit a three-run home run in the first game at the new Bronx ballpark, quickly nicknamed 'The House That Ruth Built'. It was home to the Yankees until 2008.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1955 CE <span class="tih-ago">71 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albert Einstein dies in Princeton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-einstein">Albert Einstein</a> died aged 76. His theories of special and general relativity and his work on light quanta transformed physics in the twentieth century.</p></div></li></ol>
